  ⚠️ THIS FILE IS INERT UNTIL T10. Every page still carries
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow"> and robots.txt still says
  Disallow: /. Both locks move at cutover, in the order robots.txt sets out:
  LIFT THE META TAGS FIRST, PAGE BY PAGE, THEN OPEN robots.txt. A crawler
  blocked by robots.txt cannot read a noindex tag.

  ⚠️ THREE URLs BELOW SHOULD PROBABLY NOT ALL SHIP. /healthcare/, /medical/
  and /aesthetics/ address the same buyer — the commit of 2026-09-06 records
  it as a known issue awaiting a decision and a 301. A sitemap is the wrong
  place to resolve that, so all three are listed and the duplication is named
  instead. WHICHEVER TWO SURVIVE, THE THIRD COMES OUT OF THIS FILE AND GETS A
  ROW IN _redirects. It cannot be left to the crawler to work out.

  NO <priority> AND NO <changefreq>. Google has ignored both for years.

  <lastmod> IS THE DATE THE PAGE'S CONTENT WAS LAST WRITTEN. It must be
  updated when a page changes; an always-today lastmod teaches a crawler to
  ignore the field entirely.
  ============================================================================
-->
